 "area": "scheduler",
 "description": "DEFAULT-OFF tunable seizure capability for the real engine. Adds a combinational settlement rule over a CognitiveArea lattice: overload regeneration (positive feedback, gain alpha, DEFAULT 0), a give/shed valve (give-dial), local dissipation budget, lateral symmetric diffusion over projects_to, and (V2) an EXCITATORY-RECRUITMENT coupling (gain g_rec, DEFAULT 0) over a separate `recruits` edge type: an over-threshold (ictal) neighbour injects g_rec*max(0,residual-c_gen) into this area, non-conservatively (gain-bearing, degree-scaling) -- the pro-ictal counterpart to the protective diffusive g. Writes next_residual; the engine's fold_clock_edge commits it. INERT unless an area carries a sz_managed_by edge to a SeizureConfig with sz_enabled=1 -> normal cognition byte-identical when absent/off. No new Rust Term.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "seizure_dynamics",
  "description": "un-dissipated synchronous residual as a give-failure of async settlement (glass-box, tunable, default off)"
 },
